e  any downtime during resizing  and need to be able to fetch the latest  updates from each read replica  cloud sql wasn't the perfect choice and  once you reach a certain database size  or  4000 concurrent connections it might be  time to look at another option  so let's turn things up a notch when you  want the ability to go from small to  massive scale  spanner is your answer as a fully  managed relational database service  it handles nearly unlimited horizontal  scaling for you  it's also got automatic data sharding  and replication giving you that 99.99  uptime that your data admins and users  are so fond of  and while spanner is the backbone of  billion user services like gmail and  youtube  it might be a little too powerful for  critter junction's new mini-game alone  so let's reel it back in a bit to find a  better match  cloud firestore sits a little further  towards the opposite end of the spectrum  it'll handle horizontal scaling for you  but where spanner focuses on global  consistency availability and volume  firestore also focuses on developer  flexibility  specifically firestore can sync your  data directly with client applications  through real-time listeners and support  your hierarchical data structures with  real-time querying  and offline support firestore scales up  automatically with no downtime this lets  firestore handle  thousands of requests per second  millions of concurrent connections  automatic data replication and strong  consistency  this means firestore could offer the  flexibility that our critter junction  game devs need  while also giving them the scale for  their application size  sounds like a win for firestore while  firestore might be great to handle  things like configurations  friends lists and game services it's a  novice when it comes to big data  and for critter junctions analytics team  that's a big deal  as they need a separate database system  for their needs  but that's something we'll talk about in  the next episode 